From: "copilot-swe-agent[bot]" <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:15:25 +0000
Subject: powerpc autobuild

On the powerpc autobuilders, the running kernel might be 64-bit even
if the build is in a 32-bit environment. So accept more powerpc kernel
machine names.
---
 config/_arch-n-opsys | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
 mode change 100644 => 100755 config/_arch-n-opsys

diff --git a/config/_arch-n-opsys b/config/_arch-n-opsys
old mode 100644
new mode 100755
index e0c262d..6180c70
--- a/config/_arch-n-opsys
+++ b/config/_arch-n-opsys
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@ case `uname -s` in
       x86_64)
 	ARCH=$(pick_arch x86 amd64)
 	;;
-      ppc)
+      ppc* | powerpc*)
 	ARCH=$(pick_arch ppc ppc64)
 	case `uname -r` in
 	  *osfmach*) OPSYS=mklinux ;;
